## 3. Exact Detector Classification

Let

\[
 \Gamma_a^+=c_a+c_a^\dagger,\qquad
 B_a=i\Gamma_t\Gamma_a^+,\qquad
 J(n)=\sum_{a=1}^3 n_aB_a,\qquad n\in\mathbb R^3.
\]

For real `n`, the Clifford relations give

\[
 J(n)^\dagger=J(n),\qquad J(n)^2=\lVert n\rVert^2I.
\]

Nondemolition compatibility with the frozen event context requires

\[
 [J(n),O_1]=[J(n),O_2]=0.
\]

Flattening both `16 x 16` commutators gives an exact `512 x 3` real-linear
constraint matrix.  The runner derives

\[
 \operatorname{rank}C=2,qquad
 \ker C=\operatorname{span}\{(0,0,1)\}.
\]

After normalization and quotienting the sign that merely exchanges pointer
labels, the unique detector orientation is

\[
 J=i\Gamma_t\Gamma_3^+.
\]

It is a Hermitian involution and commutes with all four `E_st`.  The entire
three-generator family transforms covariantly under all 24 proper-cubic
frames together with the transformed event context.  Literal D4 coordinate
time reflection fixes the spatial event context and sends `J` to `-J`.  The
distinct Block-192 OS fiber reflection also sends `J` to `-J`, relabels the
reflected event port, and exchanges the binary coherent sign.  Thus the unique
ray is an algebraic consequence of the frozen family and context, not a fit to
D1 or H1.

## 4. Complete Event Instrument And M2 Dilation

Define the event-supported partial unitaries

\[
 K_{st}=E_{st}J=JE_{st}
\]

and the eight effects on the two-sector carrier

\[
 F_{st,\sigma}={1\over2}
 \begin{pmatrix}
 E_{st}&\sigma K_{st}\\
 \sigma K_{st}^\dagger&E_{st}
 \end{pmatrix},\qquad \sigma=\pm1.
\]

The runner checks that every effect is a rank-four projector, all 28 distinct
cross products vanish, the eight effects sum to `I_32`, their signed pairs
coarsen to `diag(E_st,E_st)`, and the maximally mixed baseline weights are all
`1/8`.

This PVM has an explicit binary pointer dilation rather than only an abstract
effect representation.  Let

\[
 S_J=\begin{pmatrix}0&J\\J&0\end{pmatrix},\qquad
 P_\pm={I\pm S_J\over2},\qquad
 Q_\pm={I\pm Z\over2}
\]

and freeze

\[
 W=P_+\otimes I_2+P_-\otimes X.
\]

Then

\[
 W^\dagger W=WW^\dagger=I_{64},\qquad Q_+Q_-=0.
\]

`W` is nonidentity and flips an initially `Q_+` pointer exactly on the minus
branch.  Pulling back the joint readout `diag(E_st,E_st) tensor Q_sigma`
through `W` reproduces `F_st,sigma` exactly.  The four `E_st` ports plus the
one pointer bit give eight joint labels; the pointer bit alone is not claimed
to encode eight outcomes.

